    "body": "## Motivation\n\nWhen only an up-projection config is available, `get_moe_configs(..., down_moe=True)` reuses its tile parameters. An up config with `USE_TMA=true` currently also enables down TMA through this fallback, despite the documented `without TMA` behavior. This changes the intermediate buffers to expert-sorted order and changes the up GEMM's `c_sorted` setting without a separate down-projection opt-in.\n\n## Modifications\n\nCopy the fallback configurations while omitting the projection-specific `USE_TMA` key. Preserve the cached up configurations and their TMA setting. Explicit down configuration files continue to retain their own `USE_TMA` value.\n\nRegression tests cover exact-version and cross-version fallback, preservation of the cached up config, the prepared runtime up/down flags, and explicit down TMA on/off settings. The fallback test fails on the original code.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\n- `python3 -m pytest test/registered/unit/layers/moe/test_fused_moe_triton_config.py -q`: **5 passed**.\n- **31 H100 cases passed** using checkpoint-identical layer-zero weights/scales from `Qwen/Qwen3-30B-A3B-FP8@d206ba732169f29bb77fbf80fc2c4b81d4d30782`. Checked the actual file resolver for an up-only TMA config and an explicitly enabled down TMA config. Coverage: M=1,4,16,128,512,1024,4096; random, balanced and hot routes; one captured M=128 fixture; four weight-address copies.\n- All cases passed finite-output checks, BF16 output agreement against the default FP8 expert path (`rtol=atol=0.05`), and the FP32 reference guard (`candidate relative-L2 <= default relative-L2 * 1.10 + 0.0001`; dequantized checkpoint weights, TF32 disabled).\n- CUDA Graph replay matched eager execution exactly after changes to hidden states, expert IDs and routing weights.\n\nGPU checks used Torch 2.14.1+cu130, Triton 3.8.0, and `lmsysorg/sglang@sha256:ee3db420aca91ad0c7a745471b61264f76cffeb027df1d96117d95fbcb7a70a4`. The measurements cover the expert path; they do not establish full-model quality equivalence.\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\nThis restores independent TMA opt-in. Performance tuning is tracked separately.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Changed files pass all applicable pre-commit hooks.\n- [x] Added regression coverage to the registered CPU test suite.\n- [x] Kept the existing fallback contract and clarified it in the code comment.\n- [x] Provided scoped numerical and CUDA Graph validation results.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #37495124027](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/37495124027)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #37495123622](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/37495123622)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #37495124145](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/37495124145)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->\n## Public GPU validation evidence\n\n[Raw 31-case H100 results, manifests and scoped validation summary](https://gist.github.com/YzXiao101/72639c7f28c0988ebde551454dfddc87). Files `bugfix-up-only-gpu.*`, `bugfix-explicit-down-gpu.*` and `bugfix-validation-summary.json` belong to this fallback fix. The separate configuration-tuning and full-model results in the same bundle do not establish model quality or speed for this fix.\n",
